{
  "id": "mirror-writing",
  "term": "mirror writing",
  "definition": "Mirror writing is handwriting reversed so that it looks normal when viewed in a mirror. It can appear in children whose writing is still developing and in left-hand writing by many right-handed adults, especially when the hand copies the movement pattern of the other hand rather than the usual visual form of the letters.",
